1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,060
It's almost midnight, and Vasu just found a backend role at Amazon worth the effort.

2
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:07,520
Now, the real work begins.

3
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,380
Judge the fit. Prove every claim.

4
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:16,060
Find the right people. Write real messages. Remember every follow-up.

5
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,820
One opening quietly became five more jobs.

6
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,840
So which role actually deserves tonight?

7
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,480
Job Hunt Signal starts with a single résumé.

8
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:30,820
Vasu's experience becomes one private, reusable profile.

9
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:39,260
AWS event pipelines, OAuth, SCIM, production debugging, and evidence-backed achievements.

10
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:46,860
The original file is discarded after extraction, and the app only asks for context a résumé cannot know.

11
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:52,040
Then he opens Today: a ranked action queue, not another feed.

12
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:57,140
First-party openings are cleaned, deduplicated, and balanced across companies.

13
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:02,940
Each card explains eligibility, confidence, matching evidence, and real gaps.

14
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:10,100
Here is the actual Amazon opening, marked Promising because the saved description overlaps his approved evidence.

15
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:15,120
Inside the dossier, every requirement is checked before materials unlock.

16
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:21,920
When proof is missing, the claim stays unsupported and the materials stay locked. That is the feature.

17
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:29,640
A strong application still disappears without a human path, so Job Hunt Signal finds up to five appropriate people.

18
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:35,020
Peers, a manager, and a recruiter—with the public source beside every lead.

19
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:38,700
It drafts a distinct, grounded note for each one.

20
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,880
Vasu verifies, edits, and sends it himself.

21
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:45,980
The app invents nobody and sends nothing on its own.

22
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:51,800
Applications, outreach, follow-ups, and next dates live on one durable timeline.

23
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:56,200
Weekly Review shows real movement without calling silence a rejection.

24
00:01:57,160 --> 00:02:00,540
A spreadsheet remembers rows. This system remembers decisions.

25
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:07,260
Job Hunt Signal was built by Codex using GPT-5.6 across Postgres, FastAPI, and Next.js.

26
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:12,660
Vasu and Arpita made the product calls.

27
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:20,540
Fit first. Five evidence-backed paths. Résumé-first onboarding. Normal accounts. No invented claims.

28
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:27,120
GPT-5.6 helped build the product. It does not secretly score users in production.

29
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:30,340
The system does the repetition and the grounding.

30
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:34,320
Vasu keeps the judgment, the relationships, and the final click.

31
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:36,760
One résumé. Better priorities.

